# HUD & In-Game UI Improvement Plan

## Current State

- **Stack:** Expo / React Native, no UI library; `StyleSheet` + hardcoded hex colors.
- **HUD:** Shared `GameHudPanel` (full width, top radius only) — `GameHudNav` + game scoreboard + `ShotControls` inside one dark-green panel flush with the playboard.
- **Layout budget:** `BOARD_UI_GAP = 180` (`hud.chromeHeight` in `theme.ts`); **fixed** — board layout does not use dynamic `onLayout` (prevents size jump when charging).
- **Navigation:** `GameHudNav` — back + restart with confirm; no turn text in nav (turn in scoreboard center).
- **Scoreboard:** `BilliardsScoreboard` / `FourBallScoreboard` — dark felt cards, marble dots, accent bar for active player.
- **Controls:** `ShotControls` — compact side-by-side `SegmentedControl` (spin | english), `PowerMeter` when charging, `AiThinkingIndicator` for AI turn.
- **Win state:** Inline gold `winBanner` below HUD (**Phase 4** → overlay modal on dimmed table).
- **i18n:** `t(lang, …)` for nav, scoreboard, controls; spin/english labels EN/KO.
- **AI:** Shared `src/game/ai/` module; `aiLevel` in Settings. Wall-first 3-cushion routing — see Phase 1.5.

### HUD layout today

| Row | Content |
|-----|---------|
| A | Back + Restart (nav only) |
| B | Scoreboard — P1 \| stats + turn \| P2/AI |
| C | Spin + English segmented controls / power meter / AI thinking |

### Still dated (Phase 4+)

- Inline win banner pushes layout above table
- Intro screen + Settings use light gray cards, not `theme` tokens
- Win banner emoji labels (scoreboard already uses marble dots)

